      {
        "id": 90888,
        "name": "Bas",
        "username": "Bas",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/a587f6/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-07-27T07:07:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No evidence to support Guise. No evidence to support anything, though. I Can see Treacherous Ape in the sillhouette, but no idea whats up with the glowing shard and beam of light.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Something that struck me the other day is that the silhouette of treacherous ape mimicc the silhouette of Chronoranger. Furthermore, when looking at other cards featuring Treacherous ape, the stance is kind of reminiscent of a cowboy and possibly watching over the Dreamer. Keeping this in mind, could it be that the ape is the Dreamers interpretation of Chronoranger? And running away with this, has Chronoranger been keeping an eye on the Dreamer?</p>",
